{"task_id": "HumanEval/43", "solution": "def pairs_sum_to_zero(l):\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if there are two distinct elements in the list that sum to zero.\n    It uses a set for efficient O(N) average time complexity.\n    \"\"\"\n    seen_numbers = set()\n    for num in l:\n        complement = -num\n        if complement in seen_numbers:\n            return True\n        seen_numbers.add(num)\n    return False"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/43", "solution": "def pairs_sum_to_zero(l):\n    \"\"\"\n    pairs_sum_to_zero takes a list of integers as an input.\n    it returns True if there are two distinct elements in the list that\n    sum to zero, and False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    seen_numbers = set()\n    for num in l:\n        if num == 0:\n            if 0 in seen_numbers:\n                return True\n        else:\n            complement = -num\n            if complement in seen_numbers:\n                return True\n        seen_numbers.add(num)\n    return False"}
