{"task_id": "HumanEval/50", "solution": "def decode_shift(s: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Takes as input string encoded with encode_shift function. Returns decoded string.\n    \"\"\"\n    SHIFT_AMOUNT = 5\n    ALPHABET_SIZE = 26\n    base = ord('a')\n\n    decoded_chars = []\n    for char in s:\n        char_code = ord(char)\n        # Calculate the new character code by shifting back.\n        shifted_code = char_code - SHIFT_AMOUNT\n        # Handle wrapping if the shifted code goes below 'a'.\n        if shifted_code < base:\n            shifted_code += ALPHABET_SIZE\n        decoded_chars.append(chr(shifted_code))\n    return \"\".join(decoded_chars)"}
