{"task_id": "HumanEval/83", "solution": "class InvalidInputError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Custom exception for invalid input parameters.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str):\n        super().__init__(message)\n        self.message = message\ndef starts_one_ends(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Given a positive integer n, return the count of n-digit\n    positive integers that start or end with 1.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int) or n < 1:\n        raise InvalidInputError(\"Input 'n' must be a positive integer.\")\n\n    if n == 1:\n        return 1\n    else:\n        # The formula 18 * 10**(n-2) applies the inclusion-exclusion principle for n > 1.\n        # This simplifies (10**(n-1)) + (9 * 10**(n-2)) - (10**(n-2)).\n        return 18 * (10**(n - 2))"}
