{"task_id": "HumanEval/103", "solution": "def rounded_avg(n, m):\n    \"\"\"Computes the rounded average of integers in a range and returns its binary string.\n    Returns -1 if the start of the range (n) is greater than the end (m).\"\"\"\n    if n > m:\n        return -1\n\n    # Calculate sum using the arithmetic series formula for efficiency.\n    count = m - n + 1\n    total_sum = (count * (n + m)) / 2\n\n    # Compute the floating-point average.\n    average = total_sum / count\n\n    # Round the average to the nearest integer using Python's default rounding (half to even).\n    rounded_average = round(average)\n\n    # Convert the rounded average to its binary string representation.\n    return bin(rounded_average)"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/102", "solution": "def choose_num(x, y):\n    \"\"\"This function finds the largest even integer in the range [x, y] inclusive.\n    It returns -1 if no such number exists or if x > y.\n    \"\"\"\n    if x > y:\n        return -1\n\n    # Iterate downwards from y to x to find the biggest even number.\n    for i in range(y, x - 1, -1):\n        if i % 2 == 0:\n            return i\n    \n    return -1"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/103", "solution": "def rounded_avg(n, m):\n    \"\"\"You are given two positive integers n and m, and your task is to compute the\n    average of the integers from n through m (including n and m). \n    Round the answer to the nearest integer and convert that to binary.\n    If n is greater than m, return -1.\n    Example:\n    rounded_avg(1, 5) => \"0b11\"\n    rounded_avg(7, 5) => -1\n    rounded_avg(10, 20) => \"0b1111\"\n    rounded_avg(20, 33) => \"0b11010\"\n    \"\"\"\n    if n > m:\n        return -1\n\n    # Calculate the sum of integers from n to m using the arithmetic series formula.\n    # This method is efficient for large ranges.\n    count = m - n + 1\n    total_sum = (count * (n + m)) // 2\n\n    # Compute the floating-point average of the range.\n    # `count` is guaranteed to be positive as `n <= m`.\n    avg_float = total_sum / count\n\n    # Round the average to the nearest integer using Python's built-in rounding.\n    # For .5, Python's `round()` rounds to the nearest even integer.\n    rounded_avg_int = round(avg_float)\n\n    # Convert the rounded integer average to its binary string representation.\n    # The `bin()` function automatically adds the \"0b\" prefix.\n    binary_str = bin(rounded_avg_int)\n\n    return binary_str"}
