{"task_id": "HumanEval/132", "solution": "class BracketError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Base exception for bracket validation errors.\"\"\"\n    pass\nclass InvalidCharacterError(BracketError):\n    \"\"\"Raised when the input string contains invalid characters.\"\"\"\n    pass\ndef is_nested(string):\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if a string of square brackets contains a valid nested subsequence.\n    A subsequence is nested if it contains a pattern like `[[...]]` or `[[...][...]]`.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(string, str):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a string.\")\n\n    VALID_BRACKET_CHARS = {'[', ']'}\n    for char in string:\n        if char not in VALID_BRACKET_CHARS:\n            raise InvalidCharacterError(f\"Invalid character '{char}' found. Only '[' and ']' are allowed.\")\n\n    open_brackets_seen = 0\n    for char in string:\n        if char == '[':\n            open_brackets_seen += 1\n        elif char == ']':\n            # If at least two brackets are open and a closing bracket is encountered,\n            # it signifies a nested structure.\n            if open_brackets_seen >= 2:\n                return True\n            # Decrement, ensuring the count does not go negative for unmatched closing brackets.\n            open_brackets_seen = max(0, open_brackets_seen - 1)\n\n    return False"}
