{"task_id": "HumanEval/136", "solution": "def largest_smallest_integers(lst: list[int]) -> tuple[int | None, int | None]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the largest negative and smallest positive integers in a list.\n    Returns (largest_negative, smallest_positive), with None for missing values.\n    \"\"\"\n    largest_negative = None\n    smallest_positive = None\n\n    for num in lst:\n        if num < 0:\n            if largest_negative is None or num > largest_negative:\n                largest_negative = num\n        elif num > 0:  # Zero is neither positive nor negative.\n            if smallest_positive is None or num < smallest_positive:\n                smallest_positive = num\n\n    return (largest_negative, smallest_positive)"}
