{"task_id": "HumanEval/147", "solution": "class MathHelpers:\n    @staticmethod\n    def n_choose_3(n: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Calculates 'n choose 3' combinations.\n        Returns 0 if n < 3.\n        \"\"\"\n        if n < 3:\n            return 0\n        return (n * (n - 1) * (n - 2)) // 6\nclass TripleCounterService:\n    def count_valid_triples(self, n: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Calculates the total number of triples (a[i], a[j], a[k]) such that i < j < k and (a[i] + a[j] + a[k]) % 3 == 0.\n        It uses remainder counts and combinations.\n        \"\"\"\n        if n < 3:\n            return 0\n\n        rem_0_count, rem_1_count = self._get_remainder_counts(n)\n\n        combinations_000 = MathHelpers.n_choose_3(rem_0_count)\n        combinations_111 = MathHelpers.n_choose_3(rem_1_count)\n\n        return combinations_000 + combinations_111\n\n    def _get_remainder_counts(self, n: int) -> tuple[int, int]:\n        \"\"\"\n        Determines the number of elements in array `a` (from 1 to `n`) that have a remainder of 0 or 1 when divided by 3.\n        It returns counts for remainder 0 and remainder 1.\n        \"\"\"\n        rem_0_count = 0\n        rem_1_count = 0\n\n        # a[i] = i*i - i + 1\n        # Pattern of a[i] % 3 based on i % 3:\n        # if i % 3 == 0: a[i] % 3 = (0 - 0 + 1) % 3 = 1\n        # if i % 3 == 1: a[i] % 3 = (1 - 1 + 1) % 3 = 1\n        # if i % 3 == 2: a[i] % 3 = (4 - 2 + 1) % 3 = 3 % 3 = 0\n        for i in range(1, n + 1):\n            if i % 3 == 2:\n                rem_0_count += 1\n            else: # i % 3 == 0 or i % 3 == 1\n                rem_1_count += 1\n        return rem_0_count, rem_1_count\ndef get_max_triples(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    You are given a positive integer n. You have to create an integer array a of length n.\n        For each i (1 \u2264 i \u2264 n), the value of a[i] = i * i - i + 1.\n        Return the number of triples (a[i], a[j], a[k]) of a where i < j < k, \n    and a[i] + a[j] + a[k] is a multiple of 3.\n\n    Example :\n        Input: n = 5\n        Output: 1\n        Explanation: \n        a = [1, 3, 7, 13, 21]\n        The only valid triple is (1, 7, 13).\n    \"\"\"\n    service = TripleCounterService()\n    return service.count_valid_triples(n)"}
