{"task_id": "HumanEval/134", "solution": "def check_if_last_char_is_a_letter(txt: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the last character of a string is an alphabetical letter and not part of a word.\n    A word is defined as characters separated by a space.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not txt:\n        return False\n\n    last_char = txt[-1]\n\n    if not last_char.isalpha():\n        return False\n\n    # If it's a single-character letter, it's considered isolated.\n    if len(txt) == 1:\n        return True\n\n    pre_last_char = txt[-2]\n\n    # Returns True if the preceding character is a space, indicating isolation.\n    return pre_last_char.isspace()"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/151", "solution": "def double_the_difference(lst):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of squares of odd, positive integers in a list.\n    Non-integers, negative numbers, and zero are ignored.\n    \"\"\"\n    sum_of_squares = 0\n    for item in lst:\n        # Check if the item is an integer.\n        if isinstance(item, int):\n            # Check if the integer is positive and odd.\n            if item > 0 and item % 2 != 0:\n                sum_of_squares += item * item\n    return sum_of_squares"}
