{"task_id": "HumanEval/153", "solution": "def Strongest_Extension(class_name: str, extensions: list[str]) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Finds the strongest extension for a given class name based on CAP - SM rule.\n    Returns a formatted string 'ClassName.StrongestExtensionName', handling ties by first appearance.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    class Extension:\n        def __init__(self, name: str, strength: int):\n            self.name = name\n            self.strength = strength\n\n    class ExtensionStrengthCalculator:\n        def calculate(self, extension_name: str) -> int:\n            if not isinstance(extension_name, str):\n                raise TypeError(\"Extension name must be a string.\")\n            cap_count = sum(1 for char in extension_name if 'A' <= char <= 'Z')\n            sm_count = sum(1 for char in extension_name if 'a' <= char <= 'z')\n            return cap_count - sm_count\n\n    class StrongestExtensionFinder:\n        def __init__(self, calculator: ExtensionStrengthCalculator):\n            self._calculator = calculator\n\n        def find(self, extensions: list[str]) -> str:\n            if not extensions:\n                raise ValueError(\"Extensions list cannot be empty.\")\n\n            strongest_ext: Extension | None = None\n\n            for ext_name in extensions:\n                if not isinstance(ext_name, str):\n                    raise TypeError(\"All extensions must be strings.\")\n                \n                strength = self._calculator.calculate(ext_name)\n                \n                # If current extension is strictly stronger, or if it's the first candidate.\n                # Tie-breaking: if strengths are equal, the first encountered is kept implicitly.\n                if strongest_ext is None or strength > strongest_ext.strength:\n                    strongest_ext = Extension(name=ext_name, strength=strength)\n\n            # At this point, strongest_ext will always be set as extensions list is not empty.\n            return strongest_ext.name\n\n    class StrongestExtensionService:\n        def __init__(self, finder: StrongestExtensionFinder):\n            self._finder = finder\n\n        def strongest_extension_logic(self, class_name: str, extensions: list[str]) -> str:\n            if not isinstance(class_name, str):\n                raise TypeError(\"Class name must be a string.\")\n\n            strongest_ext_name = self._finder.find(extensions)\n            return f\"{class_name}.{strongest_ext_name}\"\n\n    # Instantiate components and execute the service logic.\n    calculator = ExtensionStrengthCalculator()\n    finder = StrongestExtensionFinder(calculator)\n    service = StrongestExtensionService(finder)\n    return service.strongest_extension_logic(class_name, extensions)"}
